1
00:00:03,810 --> 00:00:05,270
What's our next class again?

2
00:00:05,270 --> 00:00:06,480
Math?

3
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:08,940
When are we ever gonna use that stuff, anyway?

4
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:09,940
I know, right?

5
00:00:10,610 --> 00:00:13,360
Hey, don't touch the do!

6
00:00:17,830 --> 00:00:18,790
Every time our eyes met,

7
00:00:19,910 --> 00:00:23,290
we averted our gazes at first...

8
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:29,250
...and then looked back at each other.

9
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:34,840
That was me and Kou in our first year of middle school.

10
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,300
No one knows...

11
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:42,930
...about our awkward days together.

12
00:00:48,310 --> 00:00:52,190
The world has fallen in love

13
00:00:52,190 --> 00:00:55,860
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

14
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:59,160
I just want to understand you

15
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:03,540
Won't you open up to me?

16
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:14,670
A fumbled exchange of words leaves a little taste of regret

17
00:01:16,130 --> 00:01:18,010
Enough to make me cry

18
00:01:18,010 --> 00:01:23,350
I want to link my racing emotions to the beat of my heart

19
00:01:23,350 --> 00:01:30,480
and put it all in tune

20
00:01:32,650 --> 00:01:36,320
I lost sight of everything but my goal

21
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:39,990
and had something important fade away

22
00:01:39,990 --> 00:01:46,250
Let's start all over

23
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:51,380
The world has fallen in love

24
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:54,630
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

25
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:58,220
I want to know everything about you

26
00:01:58,220 --> 00:02:02,390
Won't you tell me more?

27
00:02:02,390 --> 00:02:06,020
One inch feels like a million miles

28
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:08,940
as the days just seem to race by

29
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:13,360
I won't and can't ever forget

30
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:16,610
this brightest page of my life.

31
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:20,450
I want to see Kou.

32
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:23,280
I want to talk to Kou!

33
00:02:26,250 --> 00:02:28,580
The advanced track's shoe lockers...

34
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:30,330
Who're you looking for?

35
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:37,340
Kou!

36
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:42,300
I've been looking for you.

37
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:44,180
There's something I want to talk to you about.

38
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:47,140
What, you make up with your friends or something?

39
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:50,230
Nah, that plan went down the drain.

40
00:02:50,230 --> 00:02:55,400
But you know, sometimes things just don't go your way.

41
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,940
That's when you go back to step one.

42
00:02:58,610 --> 00:03:00,360
And there's nothing wrong with that.

43
00:03:03,030 --> 00:03:04,330
I'm glad.

44
00:03:05,990 --> 00:03:07,120
Kou!

45
00:03:08,910 --> 00:03:12,000
I wasn't done talking to you yet...

46
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:14,500
You're the girl from before!

47
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:16,630
Oh, hey there.

48
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:19,470
What more do you have to say?

49
00:03:19,470 --> 00:03:20,840
Get off my case.

50
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:23,260
No, this is something else.

51
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:28,220
I'm coming over to make dinner today, so make sure you're home.

52
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:33,440
I'll be staying the night, too.

53
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:34,520
Staying?!

54
00:03:35,690 --> 00:03:37,320
Wait, all night?

55
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:39,990
Th-They're in that kind of relationship?

56
00:03:40,570 --> 00:03:43,110
Stupid, what are you imagining?

57
00:03:46,030 --> 00:03:47,120
We're brothers.

58
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:53,920
It's not a secret or anything, but we don't go out of our way to tell people either.

59
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:56,250
Most people have no idea.

60
00:03:57,630 --> 00:04:00,800
Brothers?! No wonder they look alike!

61
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:03,050
So, are you two dating?

62
00:04:04,140 --> 00:04:08,260
Excuse me? You really think I'd date a pig who eats more than me?

63
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:12,230
You're the one who said you liked me back in middle school!

64
00:04:13,310 --> 00:04:14,980
Wasn't that you?

65
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:17,320
You said you liked me back!

66
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:19,900
Oh, that time? You thought I was serious?

67
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:21,110
I just went with the flow.

68
00:04:21,110 --> 00:04:24,860
What?! We gazed at each other all the time back then too!

69
00:04:24,860 --> 00:04:27,950
Only 'cause you kept staring at me.

70
00:04:30,910 --> 00:04:32,160
How stupid.

71
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:34,710
In any case, none of that matters now.

72
00:04:34,710 --> 00:04:35,880
Don't run!

73
00:04:37,130 --> 00:04:39,920
One way or another, you two seem to get along well.

74
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,340
Anyway, what's your name?

75
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:44,340
Yoshioka Futaba.

76
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:46,840
That's a nice name.

77
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:48,180
Futaba, huh.

78
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:51,270
Futaba?

79
00:04:51,270 --> 00:04:52,810
Futaba...

80
00:04:55,390 --> 00:04:58,440
Oh! You're Futaba-san!

81
00:04:58,440 --> 00:05:01,400
There's a teacher hitting on a student over here.

82
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:06,820
Wait, he's joking!

83
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:14,500
Come on, I wouldn't do that!

84
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:19,340
Geez...

85
00:05:20,710 --> 00:05:22,420
So she's Yoshioka Futaba.

86
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:30,140
Yoshioka Futaba

87
00:05:35,350 --> 00:05:36,980
Yoshioka Futaba.

88
00:05:37,810 --> 00:05:38,810
Who's that?

89
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:42,280
Don't look!

90
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:44,280
What, is she your crush?

91
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:45,990
Just leave me alone!

92
00:05:49,950 --> 00:05:51,120
I see now.

93
00:05:54,450 --> 00:05:57,830
It sounds like you and Tanaka-sensei don't live together.

94
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,250
He teaches at the school I go to, so you'd think so.

95
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:05,130
Do you have your own place then?

96
00:06:05,130 --> 00:06:07,760
No, but my brother does.

97
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:10,300
So are you back at your old house now?

98
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:13,390
With your mom?

99
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:15,890
It's just me.

100
00:06:15,890 --> 00:06:17,980
Why don't you change your name back...

101
00:06:20,150 --> 00:06:21,690
Haven't you had enough?

102
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:25,400
Just shut up. It's none of your business.

103
00:06:26,570 --> 00:06:30,620
You can't say that when you're literally dragging me in.

104
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:41,080
I let go, so stop asking.

105
00:06:43,290 --> 00:06:44,340
Kou...

106
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:46,920
Why...

107
00:06:48,260 --> 00:06:51,840
We're looking straight at each other...

108
00:06:53,010 --> 00:06:55,970
...but it feels like he's staring right through me.

109
00:06:59,850 --> 00:07:01,810
Didn't you just ask me to let you go?

110
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:06,730
Get off of me.

111
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:11,700
Where did your feelings go, Kou?

112
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:18,830
Y-You disappear without a trace
and now you come back out of nowhere...

113
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:23,210
There are so many questions I want to ask!

114
00:07:24,090 --> 00:07:28,920
There are so many thoughts running through my head I don't know what to do!

115
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:34,260
Don't cry.

116
00:07:35,510 --> 00:07:37,220
I told you it was annoying.

117
00:07:40,230 --> 00:07:41,140
Sorry.

118
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:46,440
Kou?

119
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:47,730
On the day of that summer festival...

120
00:07:50,110 --> 00:07:54,780
Were you waiting for me at Triangle Park?

121
00:08:04,750 --> 00:08:06,090
I was waiting...

122
00:08:06,090 --> 00:08:09,130
I've always been waiting for you!

123
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:13,090
Sorry.

124
00:08:14,340 --> 00:08:18,310
I always thought... that you hated guys.

125
00:08:18,310 --> 00:08:19,680
I was just...

126
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:25,150
No, even so... I was still going to meet you at Triangle Park.

127
00:08:25,150 --> 00:08:30,030
But as soon as summer break started, my family fell apart.

128
00:08:31,070 --> 00:08:32,240
Lots of stuff happened.

129
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:42,540
I'm sorry I couldn't meet up with you that day.

130
00:08:48,290 --> 00:08:49,210
Kou...

131
00:08:50,670 --> 00:08:54,630
That's right. Kou has a lot of stuff going on in his life.

132
00:08:54,630 --> 00:08:56,970
A lot more than I have to worry about.

133
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:59,890
And still, I...

134
00:09:01,020 --> 00:09:02,180
Sorry.

135
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:05,190
I've been really insensitive.

136
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:06,980
It's okay.

137
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,610
Let's go home.

138
00:09:13,940 --> 00:09:14,700
Sure.

139
00:09:31,550 --> 00:09:34,170
Well, my house is this way.

140
00:09:34,170 --> 00:09:35,090
Alright.

141
00:09:38,430 --> 00:09:39,300
Kou.

142
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:43,430
Are you excited for dinner tonight?

143
00:09:43,430 --> 00:09:44,100
Why?

144
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:46,020
What do you mean, "why"?

145
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:49,020
Tanaka-sensei's going over to cook for you, isn't he?

146
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:52,730
Man, I almost forgot he was coming.

147
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:56,900
Have fun! Bye-bye!

148
00:10:00,370 --> 00:10:04,330
That was great! Kou told me more about himself.

149
00:10:16,550 --> 00:10:18,510
Mabuchi

150
00:10:16,550 --> 00:10:18,510
Tanaka

151
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:38,530
Kou 10 y.o.

152
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:38,530
Kou 11 y.o.

153
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:38,530
Kou 12 y.o.

154
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:38,530
Kou 8 y.o.

155
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:38,530
Kou 9 y.o.

156
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:38,530
Youichi 10 y.o.

157
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:38,530
Youichi 11 y.o.

158
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:38,530
Youichi 8 y.o.

159
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:38,530
Youichi 9 y.o.

160
00:10:39,860 --> 00:10:42,700
Your big brother's waiting for you.

161
00:10:44,490 --> 00:10:45,830
And I always will be.

162
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:08,270
That's right.

163
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:13,060
Even if you lose something, all you have to do is make it again.

164
00:11:14,570 --> 00:11:17,400
I'll be more careful from now on.

165
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:21,700
Starting today...

166
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:24,160
...I'll remake it all from step one.

167
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:28,080
Yoshioka, Yoshioka...

168
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:30,250
There I am. Class 2 it is.

169
00:11:31,170 --> 00:11:34,460
Makita Yuri

170
00:11:31,170 --> 00:11:34,630
Murao Shuuko

171
00:11:31,170 --> 00:11:34,630
Yoshioka Futaba

172
00:11:32,830 --> 00:11:34,630
It all starts today.

173
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:32,920
Makita-san...

174
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:36,960
Yoshioka Futaba

175
00:11:39,590 --> 00:11:40,590
Okay!

176
00:11:40,590 --> 00:11:41,590
I'll start it!

177
00:11:43,550 --> 00:11:44,800
Yoshioka-san.

178
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:51,810
Hell yeah! Murao!

179
00:11:51,810 --> 00:11:54,770
We're in the same class again!
Lookin' forward to it!

180
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:56,520
Sure.

181
00:11:56,520 --> 00:12:00,780
You said you didn't have any attachment to our class last year,

182
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:05,820
but I won't let you say that again after this year!

183
00:12:09,750 --> 00:12:12,460
Looks like I got stuck in the class with all the hotheads.

184
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:16,210
Kou!

185
00:12:16,210 --> 00:12:17,170
Yo.

186
00:12:20,550 --> 00:12:22,760
Hey, after school today...

187
00:12:21,670 --> 00:12:22,760
Why?

188
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:27,300
Kou and I... are in the same class?!

189
00:12:37,980 --> 00:12:39,820
Morning!

190
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:41,940
Man, it's way too early.

191
00:12:43,070 --> 00:12:44,110
I'm starting over.

192
00:12:45,950 --> 00:12:48,870
I'm through with making shallow friends

193
00:12:48,870 --> 00:12:50,870
and deceiving myself.

194
00:12:51,830 --> 00:12:55,120
Now that I'm in a new class, I'm going to rebuild everything from step one.

195
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:59,630
Hey, how's it feel to drop down to our class from the advanced track?

196
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:01,630
What do you mean?

197
00:13:02,590 --> 00:13:06,260
I bet you're pissed that you have to be in the same class as guys like us.

198
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:12,430
Man, could that question be any more laced with poison?

199
00:13:12,810 --> 00:13:16,270
Why would it bother me? I'm not even all that smart.

200
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:22,990
Back in middle school, I got really into studying for some reason.

201
00:13:22,990 --> 00:13:25,950
But when I tried to take a little break in high school,

202
00:13:26,450 --> 00:13:29,910
my grades fell right through the floor.

203
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:34,620
Mabuchi, are you really Tanaka's brother?

204
00:13:34,620 --> 00:13:35,410
Yeah.

205
00:13:35,410 --> 00:13:37,620
You do look pretty similar.

206
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:43,590
He's really good at keeping the conversation flowing and letting the mood stay chill.

207
00:13:53,470 --> 00:13:54,560
What's up?

208
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:57,140
Oh, it's nothing.

209
00:13:57,520 --> 00:14:00,360
What are you, an elementary schooler?

210
00:14:03,190 --> 00:14:05,570
I'm asking if you're an elementary schooler.

211
00:14:10,870 --> 00:14:12,580
Morning!

212
00:14:12,580 --> 00:14:13,490
Good morning.

213
00:14:13,490 --> 00:14:15,580
Hey, see that girl right there?

214
00:14:17,330 --> 00:14:20,580
I heard the girls in her class all gave her the cold shoulder last year.

215
00:14:20,580 --> 00:14:22,130
What, why?

216
00:14:22,130 --> 00:14:24,460
Dunno, but there must've been a reason.

217
00:14:28,430 --> 00:14:32,260
She's pretending that it doesn't bother her.

218
00:14:28,430 --> 00:14:32,890
forward

219
00:14:33,850 --> 00:14:36,560
People are so easily swayed.

220
00:14:37,520 --> 00:14:39,770
Myself included.

221
00:14:40,270 --> 00:14:45,150
All I need to do is make it seem like Makita-san has friends!

222
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:46,780
Hey, Makita-san!

223
00:14:48,150 --> 00:14:50,030
Take a look.

224
00:14:50,030 --> 00:14:52,450
It's the one you gave me before.

225
00:14:53,160 --> 00:14:54,790
You ended up using it.

226
00:14:55,410 --> 00:14:56,870
Thanks!

227
00:14:55,410 --> 00:14:59,120
kya

228
00:14:56,870 --> 00:14:59,120
No, thank you!

229
00:14:59,120 --> 00:15:01,790
Huh? They're having a normal conversation.

230
00:15:01,790 --> 00:15:03,630
I guess it wasn't her personality.

231
00:15:03,630 --> 00:15:07,050
Yes, going good! Just a bit more...

232
00:15:07,050 --> 00:15:09,430
Ah, it's her!

233
00:15:09,430 --> 00:15:13,050
I heard she got in a huge fight with some girls in her class last year.

234
00:15:09,430 --> 00:15:14,930
Her

235
00:15:13,050 --> 00:15:14,930
So we should look out for her?

236
00:15:14,930 --> 00:15:16,640
She looks really rough, too.

237
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:17,890
Is she a delinquent?

238
00:15:17,890 --> 00:15:19,020
Seriously?

239
00:15:19,020 --> 00:15:22,900
I'm rough on purpose, but I'm no delinquent.

240
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:26,780
Wait, now they're going to isolate me instead!

241
00:15:32,530 --> 00:15:35,910
Murao-san, g-good morning.

242
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:38,200
Morning.

243
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:42,330
She might be easier to talk to than I expected.

244
00:15:42,330 --> 00:15:42,920
Murao-s—

245
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:48,800
Don't talk to me
any more
aura

246
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:51,260
She shut me out completely!

247
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:52,760
Murao!

248
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:57,220
Morning! What'cha reading?
Got any good music playing?

249
00:16:00,730 --> 00:16:05,730
Man, Lady Luck must love us if she put us in the same class again.

250
00:16:05,730 --> 00:16:09,530
Please stop! Your fruitless advances remind me too much of myself!

251
00:16:09,530 --> 00:16:14,450
Oh yeah, and speaking of lucky, when I was at the convenience store the other day...

252
00:16:24,630 --> 00:16:27,090
It's hard to make any moves.

253
00:16:27,090 --> 00:16:29,460
So how's the new class?

254
00:16:30,050 --> 00:16:31,880
Oh, um...

255
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:37,050
Well, it's kind of all over the place.

256
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:39,810
Why don't you try running for class rep?

257
00:16:39,810 --> 00:16:40,470
Huh?

258
00:16:40,470 --> 00:16:44,770
I'm not exactly that type of person...

259
00:16:44,770 --> 00:16:48,770
High school will be over before you know it.

260
00:16:48,770 --> 00:16:52,820
Get out there and try some things that you can only do now.

261
00:17:00,290 --> 00:17:02,370
Easier said than done...

262
00:17:02,370 --> 00:17:03,500
How gloomy.

263
00:17:06,380 --> 00:17:07,790
Kou?

264
00:17:07,790 --> 00:17:09,840
Depressed already?

265
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:14,010
I can't take my first step if I have nowhere to stand.

266
00:17:16,010 --> 00:17:19,050
I'm already falling down the path to isolation.

267
00:17:20,390 --> 00:17:24,770
Well, I always knew how indecisive you were.

268
00:17:24,770 --> 00:17:28,230
That doesn't exactly cheer me up.

269
00:17:29,270 --> 00:17:31,860
And I never intended to.

270
00:17:33,820 --> 00:17:38,450
You talked big about starting over from the first step, and you're like this in less than a day?

271
00:17:38,450 --> 00:17:42,450
Life wasted no time in showing me how powerless I am.

272
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,620
What does that matter?

273
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:49,880
No one would mind if you fell apart this quickly.

274
00:17:53,840 --> 00:17:55,470
But on the flip side,

275
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:59,510
no one would mind if you kept at it either.

276
00:18:00,890 --> 00:18:04,140
I mean, it's not like anything's started for you yet.

277
00:18:05,140 --> 00:18:07,140
Just do what you want to do.

278
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:12,020
Nothing has started yet,

279
00:18:12,020 --> 00:18:13,570
nor have I started anything.

280
00:18:14,610 --> 00:18:18,240
If I really want to start something new,

281
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:21,700
then it shouldn't surprise me

282
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:25,410
Class Representative

283
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:25,410
Event Planner

284
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:25,410
that it'll take more than I've ever had to get moving.

285
00:18:25,410 --> 00:18:28,330
Nobody's going to volunteer?

286
00:18:32,790 --> 00:18:37,050
If you don't decide soon, we'll be here all day.

287
00:18:32,790 --> 00:18:38,260
Class Representative

288
00:18:32,790 --> 00:18:38,260
Event Planner

289
00:18:37,050 --> 00:18:38,260
What?

290
00:18:38,260 --> 00:18:40,760
I'm the only one with any right to complain.

291
00:18:43,100 --> 00:18:45,020
If I don't change,

292
00:18:48,690 --> 00:18:50,900
then I can't take that first step.

293
00:18:52,270 --> 00:18:54,400
Oh, Yoshioka!

294
00:18:54,980 --> 00:18:56,230
You'll do it?

295
00:18:56,230 --> 00:18:56,940
Yes!

296
00:18:57,360 --> 00:19:00,910
Then Yoshioka will be our female representative.

297
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:03,700
Yoshioka, take over from here.

298
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:05,120
Okay.

299
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:08,870
I will...

300
00:19:10,040 --> 00:19:11,420
...start it!

301
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:18,420
Yoshioka
Futaba

302
00:19:16,550 --> 00:19:18,420
Right, moving on...

303
00:19:18,420 --> 00:19:22,390
I think we should decide on our male representative.

304
00:19:22,390 --> 00:19:24,390
Any volunteers?

305
00:19:29,890 --> 00:19:33,560
Anyone who wants to make this class more fun with me!

306
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:34,900
Please raise your hand!

307
00:19:35,650 --> 00:19:37,480
Guess it's up to me...

308
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:40,610
I guess I'll do it.

309
00:19:43,490 --> 00:19:44,410
Kou!

310
00:19:47,450 --> 00:19:50,750
If there are no objections, Mabuchi-kun gets the position.

311
00:19:54,670 --> 00:19:57,050
I was a second too late...

312
00:19:57,050 --> 00:20:00,380
Mabuchi-kun, please come up and assist me.

313
00:20:01,930 --> 00:20:03,390
Kou, good luck.

314
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:05,300
What is it?

315
00:20:09,770 --> 00:20:10,810
Thanks.

316
00:20:10,810 --> 00:20:15,190
Stupid. I just wanted to finish this up quick and go home.

317
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:17,730
Let's get this done already.

318
00:20:18,610 --> 00:20:20,690
We need three event planners.

319
00:20:20,690 --> 00:20:22,490
Anyone wanna do it?

320
00:20:24,910 --> 00:20:26,950
I'll be one.

321
00:20:27,490 --> 00:20:28,330
Makita-san...

322
00:20:28,330 --> 00:20:29,750
You'll really do it?

323
00:20:29,750 --> 00:20:32,830
Thanks, you'll be a huge help!

324
00:20:34,790 --> 00:20:37,630
Alright, two to go.

325
00:20:44,180 --> 00:20:45,800
Murao-san?

326
00:20:46,390 --> 00:20:48,850
I'll be an event planner.

327
00:20:50,390 --> 00:20:54,440
If Murao-san's in, then the last spot has to go to...

328
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:56,230
Here!

329
00:20:56,230 --> 00:20:59,230
I'll be the last event planner!

330
00:20:59,230 --> 00:21:00,780
I knew it.

331
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:16,580
That finished pretty quickly. But seriously, what a strange bunch we are.

332
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:22,550
Good. You class reps and event planners will need to attend a leadership course.

333
00:21:22,550 --> 00:21:24,380
Leadership course?

334
00:21:24,380 --> 00:21:28,680
It's an overnight course. Tanaka-sensei will be leading it.

335
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:38,060
What's with that look? Got something to say?

336
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:40,520
N-Not really.

337
00:21:42,070 --> 00:21:43,320
It's starting.

338
00:21:44,280 --> 00:21:45,570
I'm starting it!

339
00:21:45,570 --> 00:21:47,490
This is something I can only do now.

340
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:52,200
Only at this moment, only with these people!

341
00:22:00,670 --> 00:22:05,800
In a town beset by a sudden shower,

342
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:11,180
I say "See you later", and wave goodbye.

343
00:22:11,180 --> 00:22:16,640
As I watch you pass through the ticket gate, I think:

344
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:21,940
"It never goes according to plan, does it?"

345
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:31,660
Everything seemed incredibly fragile that day,

346
00:22:31,660 --> 00:22:37,250
but it passed, as days tend to do.

347
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:47,800
The rails carry you away

348
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:56,060
leaving me alone on our usual path.

349
00:22:57,180 --> 00:23:06,690
The words I prepared for you are so simple,

350
00:23:06,690 --> 00:23:15,410
so why can't I say them?

351
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:22,380
Why can't I?

352
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:39,940
NEXT TIME...

353
00:23:27,010 --> 00:23:29,170
When we look back on this,

354
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:32,260
I want everyone who shared this experience

355
00:23:33,220 --> 00:23:37,270
to remember these warm and fun times.
